   "# Collect policy acknowledgements with a dated record",
   "Published November 2, 2026. Outsourced Employment records this step with the employee ID, the effective date, the HR reviewer, and the destination HR system; case note 1 stays with the employee file.",
   "A practical outsourced employment guide for US employers and HR operations teams, focused on policy acknowledgement with dated evidence and clear decision rights. Outsourced Employment records this step with the employee ID, the effective date, the HR reviewer, and the destination HR system; case note 2 stays with the employee file.",
   "## The control this policy acknowledgement needs",
   "Outsourced Employment keeps policy acknowledgement visible because an employee record can look complete while the effective date, the approval, and the destination system disagree. The HR operations lead needs one dated trail that shows what was checked and who accepted the change. The HR coordinator also checks the employee record, the effective date, the approval, and the destination system before the case leaves the queue. For policy acknowledgement, the written sequence ends with a named reviewer and a date before HR releases the result. Outsourced Employment records this step with the employee ID, the effective date, the HR reviewer, and the destination HR system; case note 3 stays with the employee file.",
