   "Outsourced Employment keeps policy acknowledgement visible because an employee record can look complete while the effective date, the approval, and the destination system disagree. The HR operations lead needs one dated trail that shows what was checked and who accepted the change. The HR coordinator also checks the employee record, the effective date, the approval, and the destination system before the case leaves the queue. For policy acknowledgement, the written sequence ends with a named reviewer and a date before HR releases the result. Outsourced Employment records this step with the employee ID, the effective date, the HR reviewer, and the destination HR system; case note 5 stays with the employee file.",
   "## What the policy acknowledgement record must show",
   "The policy acknowledgement record connects the employee, the effective date, the source document, the reviewer, and the destination field. Missing and confirmed-negative evidence stay separate so a blank is not reported as a clean record. The onboarding packet keeps the offer, the tax form, the policy acknowledgement, the access request, and the first-day check together. For policy acknowledgement, the written sequence ends with a named reviewer and a date before HR releases the result. Outsourced Employment records this step with the employee ID, the effective date, the HR reviewer, and the destination HR system; case note 6 stays with the employee file.",
