   "The policy acknowledgement record connects the employee, the effective date, the source document, the reviewer, and the destination field. Missing and confirmed-negative evidence stay separate so a blank is not reported as a clean record. The onboarding packet keeps the offer, the tax form, the policy acknowledgement, the access request, and the first-day check together. For policy acknowledgement, the written sequence ends with a named reviewer and a date before HR releases the result. Outsourced Employment records this step with the employee ID, the effective date, the HR reviewer, and the destination HR system; case note 8 stays with the employee file.",
   "## Where the VA's work stops",
   "The outsourced employment coordinator may prepare the policy acknowledgement packet, but employment status, pay, benefits eligibility, discipline, and policy decisions stay with the employer's accountable HR role. The coordinator names the gap and the next check. The leave record shows the request date, the policy, the balance, the approver, and the return date. For policy acknowledgement, the written sequence ends with a named reviewer and a date before HR releases the result. Outsourced Employment records this step with the employee ID, the effective date, the HR reviewer, and the destination HR system; case note 9 stays with the employee file.",
   "The outsourced employment coordinator may prepare the policy acknowledgement packet, but employment status, pay, benefits eligibility, discipline, and policy decisions stay with the employer's accountable HR role. The coordinator names the gap and the next check. The leave record shows the request date, the policy, the balance, the approver, and the return date. For policy acknowledgement, the written sequence ends with a named reviewer and a date before HR releases the result. Outsourced Employment records this step with the employee ID, the effective date, the HR reviewer, and the destination HR system; case note 10 stays with the employee file.",
   "The outsourced employment coordinator may prepare the policy acknowledgement packet, but employment status, pay, benefits eligibility, discipline, and policy decisions stay with the employer's accountable HR role. The coordinator names the gap and the next check. The leave record shows the request date, the policy, the balance, the approver, and the return date. For policy acknowledgement, the written sequence ends with a named reviewer and a date before HR releases the result. Outsourced Employment records this step with the employee ID, the effective date, the HR reviewer, and the destination HR system; case note 11 stays with the employee file.",
   "## The daily policy acknowledgement routine",
